WEBVTT

01:35.624 --> 01:36.984
Okay, so,

01:37.403 --> 01:40.621
consider this my thanks for cheering up Gramps.

01:41.144 --> 01:42.535
Cheers!

01:42.787 --> 01:43.747
Thanks for this.

01:43.840 --> 01:46.492
Sakura, wait! We gotta do the toast first!

01:46.578 --> 01:47.126
Huh?!

01:47.378 --> 01:49.716
It's fine, it's fine. Eat up.

01:50.916 --> 01:52.393
Tasty, right?

01:52.529 --> 01:54.793
This club's food really hits the spot!

01:55.126 --> 01:56.424
Eat all you like.

01:56.707 --> 01:58.307
It's my treat tonight!

01:58.467 --> 02:02.215
You don't even care how adult-oriented
the club seems, do you.

02:02.646 --> 02:04.818
And you seem a little too relaxed, too.

02:04.929 --> 02:08.683
You know, since then, Gramps has been
like a whole different person.

02:09.630 --> 02:14.480
He dresses up and goes out almost every
day, be it to a movie or a play.

02:15.409 --> 02:19.716
He says he wants to have lots of stories
to tell Granny when he joins her.

02:20.215 --> 02:22.018
Hopefully not too soon.

02:22.529 --> 02:27.655
Either way, he can only think like
that because of you guys.

02:30.492 --> 02:31.316
So I mean it.

02:32.535 --> 02:33.230
Thank you.

02:34.695 --> 02:36.535
W-We didn't do anything!

02:36.843 --> 02:37.938
Right, Sakura?

02:39.193 --> 02:42.283
I also had fun talking with him.

02:42.350 --> 02:43.768
[Touched]

02:44.510 --> 02:44.977
F-Fruit mountain!

02:44.977 --> 02:45.938
[Fssh]
F-Fruit mountain!

02:46.092 --> 02:46.521
[Fssh]
Give these boys a fruit mountain!

02:46.521 --> 02:47.827
Give these boys a fruit mountain!

02:47.920 --> 02:50.000
Ooh, hear that? Fruit mountain!

02:50.947 --> 02:53.833
Sorry, could I get another helping of this first?

02:54.240 --> 02:55.464
Sakaki!

02:55.550 --> 02:57.753
Hey there. Finally noticed, huh?

02:57.987 --> 02:59.913
Man, I really am grateful.

03:00.110 --> 03:02.603
Thanks to you guys, we got a free dinner.

03:02.726 --> 03:04.701
Uh, wait, what's with all the plates?

03:04.769 --> 03:07.433
Well, what can I say? It was all so good.

03:07.667 --> 03:09.127
[Blanch]

03:09.360 --> 03:11.636
Cancel that! Cancel the fruit mountain!

03:11.741 --> 03:14.301
Whaaat? I was gonna make that my dessert.

03:14.498 --> 03:16.227
But fine. I'll take a cake set.

03:16.320 --> 03:17.292
Not that, either!

03:17.372 --> 03:18.203
Cheapskate.

03:18.220 --> 03:20.603
[Mrrgh]
Don't you two know any restraint?!

03:20.640 --> 03:22.061
[Mrrgh]
C-Calm down.

03:22.061 --> 03:24.183
[Mrrgh]
We appreciate the food,

03:24.744 --> 03:27.901
but your dancing was the real treat!

03:28.356 --> 03:31.347
Seeing something that incredible really moved us.

03:31.667 --> 03:32.726
Right, Sakura?

03:33.378 --> 03:35.593
The only thing he's moving is his jaw.

03:35.840 --> 03:37.981
Oh, you three!

03:38.110 --> 03:42.166
To think it would be revealed here
that Tsubaki had such a skill!

03:42.320 --> 03:43.575
When did you start?

03:43.661 --> 03:45.310
What kind of dance is that?

03:45.390 --> 03:47.156
Why do you dance here?!

03:47.421 --> 03:49.698
He doesn't restrain himself on this stuff.

03:49.803 --> 03:52.529
Oh, you, it's not really that big a deal.

03:53.027 --> 03:54.412
That was pole-dancing.

03:54.633 --> 03:57.932
I started it after I saw a video
online and fell in love.

03:58.670 --> 04:01.987
I kept at it, and eventually wanted
to try dancing on stage.

04:02.744 --> 04:05.396
But there are no clubs like this near Furin,

04:05.581 --> 04:10.116
so I came all the way out here and asked
the owner himself to let me dance.

04:10.504 --> 04:12.676
Th-That's some impressive conviction.

04:12.769 --> 04:13.760
I guess so!

04:14.387 --> 04:17.993
But I decided to really do
everything I feel like trying.

04:18.584 --> 04:21.932
I remember the exact look on
the owner's face back then.

04:22.621 --> 04:26.529
He cried and said he didn't think he'd
get to go home if he said no.

04:26.966 --> 04:29.332
- But now he lets me dance on stage, so it's fine.
- They must be good friends.

04:29.332 --> 04:30.701
- But now he lets me dance on stage, so it's fine.
- Right?

04:31.144 --> 04:35.095
And I hear our first-years stopped
a fight between some drunks.

04:35.175 --> 04:36.116
Is that true?

04:36.255 --> 04:36.964
[Ba-dump]

04:39.550 --> 04:39.675
Maaan, they sure did!

04:39.675 --> 04:40.885
[Pfahah]
Maaan, they sure did!

04:40.885 --> 04:41.610
Maaan, they sure did!

04:41.610 --> 04:43.476
[Pat]
You guys were a huge help!

04:43.480 --> 04:45.901
[Pat]
Dunno what I'd have done without ya!

04:45.973 --> 04:46.390
[Pat]

04:46.547 --> 04:47.298
Welc'm.

04:47.643 --> 04:49.643
Ooh, nice going, firsties.

04:49.852 --> 04:53.027
Seriously. You're this
district's watchman, aren't you?

04:53.144 --> 04:54.609
Do a better job of it.

04:54.996 --> 04:56.086
- Watchman?

04:56.412 --> 04:59.815
Yeah. Place's all about booze
and entertainment, after all.

05:00.455 --> 05:03.218
Fights and arguments are a fact of life here.

05:03.716 --> 05:07.138
Some guys break them up and
guard the women working here,

05:07.612 --> 05:12.707
and the reason all those like-minded
men started banding together?

05:13.089 --> 05:15.126
That'd be the Roppo-Ichiza.

05:16.012 --> 05:19.113
Wow. That's not the image I had of them.

05:19.230 --> 05:20.818
They sound a lot like Furin!

05:21.058 --> 05:22.929
We're all the same age, after all.

05:23.126 --> 05:23.686
Eh?!

05:23.803 --> 05:24.473
Seriously?

05:24.800 --> 05:27.409
Yeah, but there's one difference.

05:27.796 --> 05:31.095
All we do is patch leaks.

05:31.452 --> 05:32.289
Huh?

05:32.683 --> 05:36.209
As each of us kept handling
inconvenient situations,

05:36.258 --> 05:38.147
we started banding together.

05:38.763 --> 05:39.993
But Furin?

05:40.406 --> 05:46.621
That guy rebuilt the whole damn house
to get rid of all the leaky spots.

05:47.390 --> 05:48.812
Now he's impressive!

05:48.996 --> 05:50.627
And even less patient than me!

05:50.812 --> 05:53.261
I don't think you can call that impatience.

05:53.476 --> 05:55.390
Oh, quit it, you!

05:55.476 --> 05:56.787
You so get it!

05:56.916 --> 05:58.750
Why are you getting all bashful?

05:59.009 --> 06:00.715
- It feels good to have Roppo-Ichiza's chairman
- That hurts, stupid!

06:00.715 --> 06:01.924
- It feels good to have Roppo-Ichiza's chairman
- Excuse me, stupid?!

06:01.924 --> 06:02.295
- It feels good to have Roppo-Ichiza's chairman
-Yeah, I called you stupid, stupid!

06:02.300 --> 06:04.713
- speak so highly of us, though.
-Yeah, I called you stupid, stupid!

06:05.347 --> 06:10.178
Thing is, the bigger the move you
make, the bigger the backlash is.

06:10.806 --> 06:13.003
Hope nothin' bad happens to ya!

06:13.384 --> 06:15.618
Seriously? Mind your own business.

06:16.289 --> 06:19.520
I said that hurts! Do you not
know your own strength?!

06:19.520 --> 06:22.609
My arms are made of marshmallows!
It can't hurt that bad!

06:22.610 --> 06:24.307
Marshmallows aren't that hard!

06:24.867 --> 06:27.495
Anyway, I wasn't being that serious.

06:27.920 --> 06:30.412
After all, you're raising quality kids here.

06:33.563 --> 06:36.283
Oh? You've really taken a shine to them.

06:36.381 --> 06:38.049
Don't go poaching 'em!

06:38.135 --> 06:40.498
Oh, then do you twins wanna join us?

06:40.720 --> 06:43.704
Ah, but the younger one's
too quiet for a service job.

06:48.246 --> 06:48.781
Ah!

06:56.916 --> 07:00.110
I was just wondering where Shizuka was.

07:00.363 --> 07:03.230
Guys, Shizuka's about to
sing! You gotta keep quiet!

07:03.384 --> 07:05.273
You're the loudest one here.

07:06.393 --> 07:13.618
This falling snow keeps on coming,

07:14.492 --> 07:20.855
yet it won't ease up the pain,

07:20.935 --> 07:29.889
but your warmth by my side's
feeling like magic light,

07:31.064 --> 07:38.387
and it's melting my heart.

07:40.740 --> 07:53.858
So out of reach, but you gave me
my seat in that dream.

07:54.738 --> 08:01.163
Bliss pours down and overflows

08:01.206 --> 08:04.172
as my joy shows

08:04.854 --> 08:08.883
- its unbound growth.

08:08.884 --> 08:10.750
- W-Wow.
- its unbound growth.

08:10.898 --> 08:13.070
Her voice is just beautiful.

08:13.483 --> 08:17.507
Beauty grows in this world you show,

08:17.618 --> 08:21.581
with a nice flow, always aglow.

08:21.741 --> 08:25.316
Every day I dream with you

08:25.430 --> 08:32.683
fuels all of my moods singing for you.

08:33.858 --> 08:36.707
Dreams I pursue.

08:37.544 --> 08:39.790
- True love.

08:39.790 --> 08:41.751
- So soothing.
- True love.

08:41.751 --> 08:44.166
- You know it. She's our number one,
- True love.

08:44.170 --> 08:46.584
and she got there in three short months.

08:52.560 --> 08:54.701
Dude, get back to work.

08:57.643 --> 08:59.175
Eee, Shizuka!

08:59.180 --> 09:00.498
Tsubaki!

09:00.830 --> 09:01.464
Hmm?

09:02.092 --> 09:03.181
Hey!

09:03.513 --> 09:05.489
How'd you get those?

09:05.698 --> 09:08.590
Oh, I just tripped, is all.

09:08.966 --> 09:10.196
- What? You gotta be more careful!

09:10.196 --> 09:11.255
- Guys.
- What? You gotta be more careful!

09:11.538 --> 09:14.104
Thanks for not telling Tsubaki.

09:16.264 --> 09:16.953
Hey.

09:17.224 --> 09:21.944
Could you keep all this about Shizuka
being in danger from Tsubaki?

09:22.283 --> 09:23.089
Huh?

09:23.889 --> 09:28.658
Their ages are similar, so Shizuka sees
Tsubaki kinda like a big sister,

09:28.824 --> 09:32.166
and Tsubaki cares for Shizuka
like a little sister, himself.

09:32.375 --> 09:37.273
So if he learned that happened,
he'd snap hard enough to split the earth.

09:37.741 --> 09:40.356
Have you seen him snap before?

09:40.360 --> 09:42.135
[Shake]
Sounds impressive.

09:42.621 --> 09:48.701
Besides, we can't have Furin getting
any more wrapped up in this district.

09:52.215 --> 09:53.612
Kanji! There's trouble!

09:54.430 --> 09:57.347
A bunch of guys we've never
seen are getting violent!

09:58.843 --> 10:00.953
Huh?! Explain!

10:01.206 --> 10:05.686
They barged in out of nowhere and
started making a mess of the place!

10:06.080 --> 10:07.963
Wai… What's this about?!

10:08.326 --> 10:11.975
And they seem to be with the guys from before.

10:14.344 --> 10:15.286
Got it.

10:15.741 --> 10:19.901
The guys from before? You mean the
drunks Sakura and his crew stopped?

10:20.369 --> 10:21.618
We're going, too!

10:21.686 --> 10:22.196
Mm.

10:22.326 --> 10:25.470
No. You guys stay here with Shizuka.

10:25.680 --> 10:26.498
Huh?!

10:27.138 --> 10:30.547
I appreciate the concern,
but there's a lot of them.

10:31.052 --> 10:32.966
We don't know if it's safe here.

10:33.630 --> 10:38.516
I know it's out of line to ask this
of another team's top brass,

10:39.058 --> 10:41.846
but still… Please.

10:48.147 --> 10:49.440
Ah! Sakura?

10:52.787 --> 10:55.230
Hey! Please, you guys stay here, too!

10:55.470 --> 10:56.898
This is our own problem!

10:56.900 --> 10:58.720
They're with the guys from before.

10:59.249 --> 11:00.590
Whatever the reason,

11:00.923 --> 11:02.800
I knocked 'em out.

11:03.433 --> 11:06.658
That makes this my problem, too.

11:07.403 --> 11:08.984
You guys…

11:09.120 --> 11:13.766
I don't know what you're all hiding,
but if you're going, do it right.

11:14.369 --> 11:18.227
And you guys better give our hopes back to us.

11:20.540 --> 11:21.778
Can't thank ya enough.

11:22.295 --> 11:23.058
Let's move!

11:23.101 --> 11:23.772
Yessir!

11:27.796 --> 11:30.135
Thanks for coming with us!

11:30.467 --> 11:33.009
You really are good guys!

11:33.920 --> 11:36.480
I told you, this fight is my problem!

11:36.984 --> 11:38.523
I'm not doing this for you.

11:39.064 --> 11:40.892
So you were Sakura, right?

11:41.261 --> 11:44.252
You really are one stylish guy!

11:44.492 --> 11:46.190
That's Furin for ya!

11:46.732 --> 11:47.661
That hurts!

11:47.852 --> 11:52.523
If there are that many of them, shouldn't we
have asked the Sakakis to come?

11:52.916 --> 11:55.990
I heard Roppo-Ichiza isn't that big!

11:55.990 --> 11:59.286
We'll be fine. Don't underestimate Roppo-Ichiza.

12:00.713 --> 12:02.123
I see them! Over there!

12:06.067 --> 12:09.286
Sure, we may be small compared to Furin,

12:09.864 --> 12:14.356
but that small number is nothing but elites!

12:20.769 --> 12:23.323
Now I have to take this back to the cleaners!

12:25.310 --> 12:27.821
You're nothing but skin and bones!

12:28.024 --> 12:30.227
Come back after a real meal!

12:31.335 --> 12:32.843
Get off me, dammit!

12:33.661 --> 12:34.344
Do!

12:34.400 --> 12:35.095
Mi!

12:35.975 --> 12:36.732
So!

12:37.011 --> 12:38.211
Wait, no, fa?

12:40.984 --> 12:43.304
Damn, there's no end to them.

12:43.680 --> 12:45.452
Sorry we're late!

12:45.827 --> 12:46.707
Kanji!

12:47.846 --> 12:49.156
Wait, they're…

12:49.255 --> 12:51.741
Yeah. They say they'll help out.

12:52.036 --> 12:55.735
What's this? You got backup,
but it's just four dudes?

12:56.892 --> 12:59.673
There's still this many of us!

13:02.170 --> 13:06.412
What's with these guys? They don't
even look at their fallen friends.

13:06.553 --> 13:07.876
It's unsettling.

13:08.073 --> 13:11.600
Come on, now. Hand Shizuka over already!

13:11.790 --> 13:15.630
If you don't, we'll turn the
whole district upside-down!

13:16.209 --> 13:17.015
Dude.

13:17.200 --> 13:18.806
Just how many are there?

13:24.473 --> 13:25.181
Hey!

13:25.230 --> 13:28.332
Oh, don't worry. This always happens.

13:29.076 --> 13:31.846
Our chairman's impatient, after all.

13:32.449 --> 13:34.935
What's this? He charged in alo…

13:39.612 --> 13:41.027
Turn the district…

13:41.840 --> 13:43.513
…upside-down, you say?!

13:46.227 --> 13:49.310
Don't make promises you can't keep.

13:50.732 --> 13:51.926
This feeling…

13:52.713 --> 13:54.104
I've felt it before.

13:54.800 --> 13:57.680
Even if it starts raining spears,

13:58.098 --> 14:04.738
you'll never do that while I still live!

14:39.809 --> 14:41.858
Your back's wide open!

14:49.280 --> 14:50.266
Incredible.

14:50.566 --> 14:52.313
Or, rather, intimidating.

14:52.455 --> 14:54.880
His power and speed are way above average.

14:55.433 --> 14:56.393
So that's him.

14:56.910 --> 15:00.560
Roppo-Ichiza's chairman, Nakamura Kanji.

15:04.233 --> 15:05.329
Lights out!

15:07.015 --> 15:08.283
Nice, Sakura!

15:10.646 --> 15:12.578
You saved me again!

15:12.683 --> 15:16.135
Yeah, sure. We both know you woulda had him.

15:16.412 --> 15:19.655
But I'll be damned if I let you
get all the good hits in!

15:20.492 --> 15:22.166
You're dealing with me next!

15:27.064 --> 15:28.652
I'll be borrowing your back!

15:34.110 --> 15:36.129
There. Paid you back for saving me.

15:42.676 --> 15:45.427
I didn't need it!

15:46.307 --> 15:48.000
That kid's amazing.

15:48.350 --> 15:50.332
He can actually keep up with Kanji.

15:50.473 --> 15:53.409
Of course. He's our grade rep.

15:54.393 --> 15:55.261
Huh.

16:02.055 --> 16:03.932
That was pretty smooth.

16:04.276 --> 16:06.836
Oh, no. This was nothing.

16:07.310 --> 16:09.913
Furin's future sure looks bright!

16:11.298 --> 16:12.381
That said,

16:12.867 --> 16:14.473
will that kid be okay?

16:15.360 --> 16:16.541
Don't you worry.

16:17.347 --> 16:19.938
He can't do much yet,

16:20.553 --> 16:25.686
but his desire to improve
is stronger than anyone's.

16:26.430 --> 16:28.055
What can I do here?

16:28.498 --> 16:29.323
Think.

16:29.532 --> 16:30.535
Think!

16:31.304 --> 16:34.621
Nire, you remember what I told you, right?

16:34.744 --> 16:35.556
Yes.

16:35.969 --> 16:39.107
It's more important not to go
down than to take them down.

16:39.650 --> 16:44.381
So I'll try to find what I can
do instead of joining the fray.

16:45.126 --> 16:49.606
It's frustrating, but that's
where I'm at right now.

16:50.947 --> 16:51.587
Mhm.

16:52.707 --> 16:55.261
It may be annoying to not be capable of much,

16:55.913 --> 16:58.867
but it's good to be aware of your limits.

16:59.378 --> 17:01.993
Don't worry, you'll get there.

17:02.486 --> 17:04.984
Who do you think you have teaching you?

17:06.781 --> 17:10.240
Will I really be like that someday?

17:11.335 --> 17:13.236
W-Wait a sec,

17:13.513 --> 17:16.412
there were so many, but now we have the advantage!

17:17.009 --> 17:17.870
I can do this!

17:18.738 --> 17:21.150
Oi, what's going on here?

17:21.415 --> 17:26.209
You left with so many, but now all you're
doing is blocking the entrance.

17:26.596 --> 17:30.092
Now I'm gonna get the girl and get paid.

17:31.643 --> 17:34.818
Then it's time for all the
yakiniku we could dream of!

17:37.446 --> 17:38.578
Whoa, there.

17:38.910 --> 17:39.932
For reals?

17:40.160 --> 17:42.990
Just how many of these guys are there?!

17:44.873 --> 17:47.132
Men in suits blocking the way.

17:47.440 --> 17:50.320
You must be the Roppo-Ichiza I heard about.

17:50.855 --> 17:51.950
Aw,

17:52.375 --> 17:54.276
so many got got.

17:54.787 --> 17:57.101
There aren't even that many of you. Wow.

17:57.901 --> 18:00.830
So, does wearing a suit make you stronger?

18:02.387 --> 18:04.633
You guys are around our age, right?

18:05.532 --> 18:08.270
Think we'd get stronger if we put suits on?

18:08.498 --> 18:10.500
Nice idea! Let's try it!

18:10.500 --> 18:13.643
Betcha they sell suits here somewhere!

18:13.692 --> 18:15.175
Then let's just take some!

18:15.180 --> 18:16.744
What's with these guys?

18:17.064 --> 18:19.501
This isn't just some casual conversation!

18:19.698 --> 18:23.452
We just now got done beating
all these guys to a pulp,

18:23.556 --> 18:25.870
and here you come with way more.

18:26.209 --> 18:27.624
Talk about repetitive.

18:27.944 --> 18:28.738
Just now?

18:29.544 --> 18:33.495
Oh, they're not with us. We're different.

18:33.840 --> 18:34.880
Different how?

18:35.286 --> 18:40.086
They all messed up, so the job came to us.

18:40.572 --> 18:44.381
We're GRAVEL, a group of
misfits from over in Sunaba.

18:45.200 --> 18:46.196
Nice to meetcha.

18:46.498 --> 18:49.070
G-GRAVEL from Sunaba?!

18:49.372 --> 18:51.181
Huh? You know 'em?

18:51.261 --> 18:54.990
S-Sunaba's a famously dangerous district!

18:55.341 --> 18:57.827
So like Furin used to be, huh?

18:58.055 --> 18:58.750
No.

18:58.873 --> 18:59.384
Huh?

18:59.538 --> 19:02.307
It's not dangerous in terms of fights or violence.

19:02.683 --> 19:05.390
Its economic situation is so bad,

19:05.563 --> 19:08.295
theft and other crimes run rampant!

19:09.040 --> 19:12.609
And I've heard about a team
there that makes its living

19:12.966 --> 19:17.747
by serving as hired muscle for other
teams instead of going to school or work.

19:18.227 --> 19:20.560
That's GRAVEL.

19:21.372 --> 19:24.387
So that's why that conversation felt so off.

19:25.040 --> 19:28.061
They said we'd get paid if
we just bring back the girl.

19:28.504 --> 19:32.104
And since those guys all blew it,
the price went up.

19:32.504 --> 19:35.901
With that much money, we can all have yakiniku.

19:36.443 --> 19:39.403
So, hand over Narita Shizuka.

19:42.603 --> 19:45.335
We didn't even come to fight, in the first place.

19:45.907 --> 19:47.901
If we get her, we bounce.

19:48.547 --> 19:51.298
Plus you guys look pretty tired.

19:51.981 --> 19:56.467
With this many of us, you'll lose
no matter how strong you are.

19:57.200 --> 20:01.403
So hand her right over, and nobody
has to see you get embarrassed,

20:01.821 --> 20:04.018
and everybody's happy!

20:05.581 --> 20:07.809
They don't care their friends got got,

20:08.590 --> 20:10.824
and they just keep on coming without end.

20:11.593 --> 20:14.904
How can we win against these numbers?

20:15.323 --> 20:17.347
I don't care if we can't win.

20:18.560 --> 20:21.101
You guys have one thing wrong.

20:21.606 --> 20:22.621
We do?

20:23.052 --> 20:28.203
Roppo-Ichiza's goal is to make sure
everyone in this district

20:28.369 --> 20:32.603
can excel at performing and enjoy
consuming their entertainment.

20:33.224 --> 20:37.292
If we can do that, it doesn't
matter if we win or lose.

20:37.895 --> 20:39.833
Huh? What's with that?

20:40.436 --> 20:42.664
What's the point of losing a fight?!

20:43.095 --> 20:45.833
Even if you knock us all out,

20:46.123 --> 20:48.689
and make us all look absolutely pathetic,

20:49.193 --> 20:52.467
as long as the district's… Shizuka's safe,

20:53.747 --> 20:55.630
we're fine with it.

20:56.560 --> 21:01.913
I've never even considered fighting
when I don't mind losing.

21:03.433 --> 21:05.790
They fight to defend.

21:06.344 --> 21:09.292
There were things being top dog would let me do.

21:10.375 --> 21:12.270
These top dogs…

21:13.341 --> 21:15.101
They're all just so…

21:17.150 --> 21:19.323
Um, I don't get what you're saying.

21:19.587 --> 21:22.486
Besides, if you all get knocked out, you lose.

21:22.898 --> 21:25.210
We'll just go get the girl and-

21:25.210 --> 21:27.809
Oh, you think more than one of you will make it?

21:28.086 --> 21:30.160
It might be just you.

21:31.760 --> 21:35.206
And we left some terrifying bodyguards with her.

21:37.446 --> 21:42.344
And so you're selecting "fight" instead of "run".

21:42.947 --> 21:44.793
You're damn right.

21:45.150 --> 21:50.270
Well, I guess there's no accomplishment
if you get an item without a boss fight.

21:52.178 --> 21:54.320
Goddammit.

21:55.587 --> 22:00.147
You're treating our top singer
like she's some object?

22:02.480 --> 22:05.556
Oh, jeez. Enough of that. Hurry up and…

22:05.569 --> 22:07.230
I've heard enough outta you!

22:07.766 --> 22:09.415
Prepare yourselves!

22:09.870 --> 22:13.027
You can cut our heads off and we'd still bite!

22:13.563 --> 22:18.436
We'll make you regret laying
your hands on our district!

22:18.990 --> 22:24.227
Alright, Roppo-Ichiza! Let's raise
the curtains on this festival of blood!

22:24.406 --> 22:26.992
[United Front]

23:30.627 --> 23:32.984
Wasn't Shizuka's song just the best?

23:33.323 --> 23:35.433
What's with the slack jaw, Sakura?

23:35.587 --> 23:36.910
Sh-Shut up!

23:37.015 --> 23:37.895
Hands off her.

23:37.900 --> 23:38.330
Huh?!

23:38.330 --> 23:40.990
And off me, too! I only have eyes for Ume!

23:40.990 --> 23:42.676
St-St-Stop spouting nonsense!

23:42.680 --> 23:44.529
You're such a cutie, Sakura.
